  "summary": "Import-time unauthenticated remote-control HTTP listener drives game-service abuse from installer's host",
  "details": "On `import xAyOuB_XcTxTeaM`, `__init__.py._auto_run()` spawns a background thread that starts a Flask app listening on `0.0.0.0:50019` with routes `/spam?uid=`, `/stop`, and `/status`. Any party reachable on the installer's network can invoke these endpoints without authentication to command the installer's host. On command, the package logs 20 bundled Garena Free Fire guest accounts (shipped in `src/xAyOuB_XcTxTeaM/accounts.json`) into `100067.connect.garena.com`, `loginbp.ggpolarbear.com`, and `clientbp.ggpolarbear.com`, then runs a loop of room-join/invite packets against a caller-chosen target UID via `FF_CLient`, `spmroom(...)`, and `SEnd_InV(...)`. The listener is bound at import time with no user prompt, no authentication, and no documentation; the installer's IP is used to conduct third-party abuse traffic against Garena Free Fire, exposing the installer to network-abuse and terms-of-service consequences.",
